// go.work — developer convenience across the repo's Go modules.
//
// DELIBERATE EXCLUSION: boundary/ is NOT in this workspace (skeleton design
// Part 4, resolution 17). The boundary harness is the executable specification
// (D26) — RED by design and never built together with production code; it is
// satisfied from the outside via assurance/conformance-adapter/. Keeping it
// out of go.work makes "the harness never links production packages" a
// property of the build, not a convention. Note: workspace mode makes
// cross-imports between the modules below *resolvable*, so the rule that
// proto/gen/go is the only legal cross-tree import is a convention — enforced
// by the CI import-boundary gate, not by the toolchain.
//
// boundary/ has its own go.mod and is exercised by its own CI lane
// (vet + build + compile-only test).

go 1.25.11

use (
	./assurance/conformance-adapter
	./assurance/contract-harness
	./client
	./identity/grant-service
	./orchestrator
	./proto/gen/go
	./vm
)
